P('/pratiche-edilizie-cila-scia/', hero="re-direttore-lavori",
 title="Building permits in Italy: CILA and SCIA handled for you",
 desc="CILA, SCIA, permits, site safety and tax-bonus paperwork: the building permits for your renovation in Veneto and Friuli, Italy, prepared by our technicians.",
 ogtitle="Building permits in Italy — Danova Real Estate", ogdesc="Building permits, safety and tax deduction documents: we take care of them.",
 crumbs=[RE, ("Building permits", None)], eyebrow="Building permits in Italy",
 h1=f"Building permits CILA and SCIA: {G}we handle the bureaucracy.{_G}",
 lead="Planning check, CILA or SCIA, safety notices and plans, public land occupation, end-of-works filings and documents for tax deductions: our technicians prepare everything needed before, during and after the works.",
 cta1="Let’s check your case", cta2="Which permit you need",
 sezioni=[
  {"id": "in-breve", "tipo": "breve", "eyebrow": "In short", "h2": f"Which permit {G}your works need{_G}",
   "testo": "As a general rule in Italy: <b>ordinary maintenance</b> (painting, replacing floors and tiles, repairs) is <b>free building activity</b>; <b>extraordinary maintenance</b> without structural work (moving partitions, redoing systems, joining or dividing rooms) usually requires a <b>CILA</b> (certified notice of start of works); work on <b>structural parts</b> or certain renovations requires a <b>SCIA</b> (certified report of start of activity) or a building permit. Each municipality may have its own rules and forms: that is why we always start with a technical check.",
   "fatti": [("Free activity", "Painting, floors, repairs"), ("CILA", "Partitions, systems, internal layout"), ("SCIA", "Structural work and renovations"),
             ("Safety", "Preliminary notice and plans when required"), ("End of works", "Filings and cadastral update"), ("Bonuses", "Documents and ENEA filing")]},
  {"id": "cosa", "tipo": "cards", "eyebrow": "What we do", "h2": f"All the paperwork {G}for the site{_G}",
   "corpo": [("Preliminary check", "Checking the planning and cadastral compliance of the property before works."), ("CILA and SCIA", "Preparation and filing via the municipality portal, with drawings."),
             ("Site safety", "Preliminary notice, safety plan and coordination where the law requires."), ("Public land", "Request to occupy public land for scaffolding and skips."),
             ("Opinions and constraints", "Paperwork for listed buildings and historic centres, fire safety for businesses."), ("End of works and cadastre", "End-of-works notice, cadastral update, system certificates.")]},
  {"id": "promesse", "tipo": "promesse", "eyebrow": "Guarantees", "h2": f"Permits included {G}in the fixed price{_G}"}],
 faqtitle=f"Questions about {G}building permits.{_G}",
 faq=[("What is the difference between CILA and SCIA?", "CILA is a notice for extraordinary maintenance that does not touch structures; SCIA is a certified report required for more significant work, for example on structural parts. The technician assesses which you need."),
      ("What happens if I do works without a permit?", "You risk fines and problems when selling the property, as well as losing tax deductions. That is why we prepare the paperwork before starting."),
      ("The property has irregularities: can it be renovated?", "Often yes, regularising before or during the works when possible. The preliminary check is there to find out before spending.")] + FAQ_BASE[:2],
 ctabox={"h2": "Tell us and we’ll check.", "p": "Address and the works you want to do: we tell you which permit is needed and prepare it.", "btn": "Let’s check your case"},
 altrititle="Related pages",
 altri=[("Italian renovation bonus 2026", u('/bonus-ristrutturazione-2026/')), ("Guide: CILA or SCIA", u('/guide/cila-o-scia/')), ("Turnkey renovation", u('/ristrutturazioni-chiavi-in-mano/')),
        ("General contractor", u('/general-contractor/')), ("Danova Real Estate", u('/real-estate/'))],
 svc=svc("Building permits CILA and SCIA", "Building permit services",
         "Planning check, CILA, SCIA, site safety, public land occupation, listed building paperwork, end-of-works, cadastral update and tax deduction documents in Veneto and Friuli, Italy.",
         ["Preliminary check", "CILA", "SCIA", "Site safety", "Public land", "End of works and cadastre"]))

P('/bonus-ristrutturazione-2026/', hero="re-soggiorno-nuovo",
 title="Italian renovation tax bonus 2026: 50% and 36% explained",
 desc="Italian renovation bonus 2026: 50% deduction on the main residence and 36% on other properties, €96,000 cap, ecobonus and furniture bonus. What applies and how not to lose it.",
 ogtitle="Italian renovation bonus 2026 — what applies", ogdesc="Rates, spending caps, ecobonus, furniture bonus and documents: the practical guide by Danova Real Estate.",
 crumbs=[RE, ("Renovation bonus 2026", None)], eyebrow="Italian tax deductions · updated October 2026",
 h1=f"Italian renovation bonus 2026: {G}what applies and how not to lose it.{_G}",
 lead="Italy’s 2026 Budget Law confirmed for the whole of 2026 a 50% deduction for work on the main residence and 36% on other properties. Here are rates, caps, related bonuses and the documents our technicians prepare.",
 cta1="Let’s check your bonuses", cta2="The rates",
 badges=["50% main home", "36% other properties", "€96,000 cap", "Updated October 2026"],
 sezioni=[
  {"id": "in-breve", "tipo": "breve", "eyebrow": "In short", "h2": f"Italian home bonuses {G}in 2026{_G}",
   "testo": "For expenses incurred in <b>2026</b> the Italian income tax (IRPEF) deduction for <b>building renovation</b> is <b>50% on the main residence</b> and <b>36% on other properties</b>, with a spending cap of <b>€96,000 per property unit</b>, spread over 10 annual instalments. The <b>ecobonus</b> for energy-efficiency work follows the same rates. The <b>furniture bonus</b> is extended with a cap of <b>€5,000</b>. From <b>2027</b> rates are expected to fall to <b>36% and 30%</b>. The 75% architectural barriers bonus is no longer available.",
   "fatti": [("Main residence", "50%"), ("Other properties", "36%"), ("Spending cap", "€96,000 per unit"), ("Instalments", "10 years"), ("Furniture bonus", "€5,000 cap"), ("From 2027", "36% / 30%")]},
  {"id": "quali", "tipo": "cards", "eyebrow": "Which works", "h2": f"What qualifies {G}for deductions{_G}",
   "corpo": [("Extraordinary maintenance", "Redoing systems and bathrooms, moving partitions, replacing windows with changes."), ("Building renovation", "Works that transform the property, with the required permits."),
             ("Energy efficiency (ecobonus)", "External insulation, windows, insulated roofs, efficient heating meeting the requirements (since 2025 gas-only boilers are excluded)."),
             ("Shared parts of buildings", "Work on facades, stairs and common systems, including ordinary maintenance."), ("Sismabonus", "Seismic improvement works, extended at the main-residence rates."),
             ("Furniture bonus", "Furniture and large appliances for the renovated property, €5,000 cap.")]},
  {"id": "documenti", "tipo": "passi", "eyebrow": "How not to lose it", "h2": f"The documents {G}that really matter{_G}",
   "corpo": [("Correct permit", "CILA, SCIA or declaration of free activity depending on the works: without it, the deduction is at risk."),
             ("Dedicated bank transfer", "Payments by the special transfer for deductions, with reference, beneficiary tax code and contractor VAT number."),
             ("Detailed invoices", "Invoices in the name of the person deducting, with a clear description of the works."),
             ("ENEA filing", "For the ecobonus and some renovation bonus works, within 90 days of completion."),
             ("Certifications", "Technical requirements, system compliance declarations and product data sheets.")]},
  {"id": "nota", "tipo": "testo", "eyebrow": "Important note", "h2": f"Always check {G}with your accountant{_G}",
   "corpo": ["This page summarises the rules in force in October 2026 under Italy’s 2026 Budget Law. Deductions are on Italian income tax and depend on each person’s tax situation (Italian tax liability, title to the property, residence): before deciding, consult your accountant or tax adviser.",
             "We handle the technical side: we check that the works qualify, prepare building permits, certifications and ENEA filing, and issue invoices with the correct wording. See also " + A('/pratiche-edilizie-cila-scia/', 'building permits in Italy') + "."]},
  {"id": "promesse", "tipo": "promesse", "eyebrow": "Guarantees", "h2": f"Renovate {G}with the right bonuses{_G}"}],
 faqtitle=f"Questions about the {G}2026 renovation bonus.{_G}",
 faq=[("How much can be deducted in 2026 to renovate a main residence?", "50% of expenses incurred in 2026 for the main residence, up to €96,000 per unit, recovered in 10 annual instalments."),
      ("And for a second home or a rental property?", "36%, with the same €96,000 cap."),
      ("Can a non-resident owner use these deductions?", "The deductions reduce Italian income tax (IRPEF): they are only useful if you have taxable income in Italy. Check your case with an Italian accountant."),
      ("What changes in 2027?", "Under current rules rates will fall to 36% for the main residence and 30% for other properties. Those who can bring works forward to 2026 keep the higher rates."),
      ("Are the invoice discount or credit transfer still available?", "For most new works no: today the rule is deduction in the tax return, with limited exceptions provided by law. Check your case with your accountant."),
      ("Do you handle the ENEA filing?", "Yes, for the works we carry out we prepare the ENEA filing and technical documentation.")],
 ctabox={"h2": "Use the bonuses while they are at 50%.", "p": "Tell us the property and works: we check which deductions apply and give you a fixed-price quote.", "btn": "Let’s check your bonuses"},
 altrititle="Related pages",
 altri=[("Building permits in Italy", u('/pratiche-edilizie-cila-scia/')), ("External wall insulation", u('/cappotto-termico/')), ("Flooring and windows", u('/pavimenti-e-serramenti/')),
        ("Apartment and house renovation", u('/ristrutturazione-appartamenti-e-case/')), ("Custom-made furniture", u('/mobili-su-misura/'))],
 svc=svc("Support with the Italian renovation bonus 2026", "Technical support for building tax deductions",
         "Technical check of qualifying works, building permits, certifications, ENEA filing and documentation for the 2026 Italian renovation bonus, ecobonus, sismabonus and furniture bonus in Veneto and Friuli.",
         ["Deduction check", "Building permits", "Certifications", "ENEA filing", "Furniture bonus support"]))
